2025-12-09 10:15:00	Completed OpenSpec implementation for fix-viewer-color-grouping-and-markers. Fixed two bugs: (1) Implemented position-based color mapping using regex pattern matching to handle repeated SNs correctly - now {<0853>} in different groups show different colors (pink vs purple). Modified color_mapper.js with buildRegexPattern() using [^<>{}()]+ separator, updated left_panel.js to pass groups for currentVerse only, updated right_panel.js to pass currentGroups. (2) Preserved WH/WAH/WTH prefixes in :: :: markers by removing prefix stripping in parse_verse_v1_8.py extract_interleaved_text(). Tested with Gen 1:1 - all three sections (parsed, raw, left panel) now show correct colors for repeated {<WH0853>}. Committed as v1.8.5.
2025-12-09 10:45:00	Fixed HTML escaping bug in parsed section markers. User reported markers showing ::{}天:: instead of ::{<WH0853>}天<WH08064>::. Root cause: applyColorsToParsedText() only escaped SN group part, leaving rest of line unescaped. Browser interpreted <WH0853> as HTML tags and stripped them. Fixed by escaping both snPart and restPart. Markers now correctly display with all SNs visible. Commit 91b3901.
2025-12-09 11:00:00	Fixed position-based highlighting for repeated SNs. User reported clicking heaven group {<WH0853>}<WH08064> incorrectly highlighted 3 SNs (including earth's {<WH0853>}) instead of just 2. Two root causes: (1) getSNGroupFromColorMap() used colorMap lookup with "first occurrence wins", returning wrong group for second {<WH0853>}. (2) findCorrespondingElements() matched by SN code only, finding ALL instances. Fixed by: (1) Using clicked element's actual background color to find correct group. (2) Adding color-based filtering in findCorrespondingElements(). Now clicking each group highlights only its own SNs correctly. Commit 5852e73.
