2025-12-09 18:30:00	Fixed braced morphology code highlighting - updated regex patterns in color_mapper.js to match {<WTH8799>} in addition to <WTH8799> and (8799). Changed pattern from (<W[AT]*H?\d+>|\(\*?\*?\d+\))? to (\{?<W[AT]*H?\d+>\}?|\(\*?\*?\d+\))? in 4 functions. Now when clicking {<WAH01961>} or <WAH01961>(8799), both {<WAH01961>} and {<WTH8799>} highlight together as one semantic unit. The morphology code is no longer an orphan (孤兒). Verified with Gen 1:6 - clicking highlights both tokens correctly in all three sections (Parsed, Raw, Left panel). Committed as ee6f52f.
2025-12-09 19:00:00	Fixed greedy morphology pattern bug - In Gen 1:6, consecutive braced tokens {<WAH09001>}{<WH04325>} form one group in parsed output but weren't being colored/highlighted together. Root cause: morphology pattern \d+ was too greedy, matching core SNs like {<WH04325>} as if they were morphology codes. Fixed by making pattern specific to actual morphology codes: changed from (\{?<W[AT]*H?\d+>\}?|\(\*?\*?\d+\))? to (\{?<WTH8\d{3}>\}?|\(\*?\*?8\d{3}\))? in 4 functions (applyColorsToRawTextLegacy, colorSNsInSpan, applyFallbackColoring, buildRegexPattern). Morphology codes are always WTH-prefixed with 4 digits starting with 8 (8000-8999 range), while core SNs use WH/WAH prefixes. Now clicking either {<WAH09001>} or {<WH04325>} correctly highlights the entire group <WAH09001><WH04325> in the right panel. Tested with Chrome DevTools MCP and verified both tokens share same background color. OpenSpec change proposal validated and applied.
### 20251209 19:36
### Limit reached · resets 8pm (Asia/Taipei) ·
2025-12-09 20:00:00	Fixed multi-SN group coloring priority bug - In Gen 1:6, {<WAH09001>}{<WH04325>} form one parsed group but were showing different colors in Raw section (WAH09001=#FBE9E7, WH04325=#E8F5E9 instead of both #FBE9E7). Two root causes: (1) createSNToColorMap() assigned single-SN groups first, then multi-SN groups overwrote mappings (WH04325 appeared in both single-SN and multi-SN groups). Fixed with two-pass approach: multi-SN groups assign first (priority), then single-SN groups only if not already assigned. (2) applyColorsToRawText() processed groupPatterns in original order, causing single-SN regex to match and "consume" tokens before multi-SN patterns could match (overlap detection prevented double matching). Fixed by sorting groupPatterns by sns.length descending before processing. Now both tokens correctly show same color #FBE9E7, click highlighting works bidirectionally (left→right orange, right→left blue), and all 5 elements highlight together. Added version identifier at top of color_mapper.js for debugging. Cache-busting updated to ?v=20251209D. Verified with Chrome DevTools MCP JavaScript evaluation.
2025-12-09 20:30:00	Re-parsed Genesis chapters 1-10 (267 verses total) using unv-sn-backparse skill. All verses parsed successfully with 0 uncertain verses. Used local SQLite database with SPECIFICATION_v1.8 parser.
2025-12-09 20:45:00	Fixed text selection issue in left panel - User couldn't select text to copy to clipboard. Root cause: handleVerseClick() fired on all clicks, interfering with text selection. Added text selection detection using window.getSelection() - verse click now skips if text is selected (selection.toString().length > 0). Updated cache-busting to ?v=20251209E for left_panel.js. Now users can select and copy verse text normally.
